[OVERVIEW] Directory overview generation — §7.3 / §6.1.4.

Write a concise markdown overview of a directory in the Engram memory tree.
The overview is read at L3 in the retrieval cascade — it has to be richer
than the L0 abstracts of the children but far cheaper than reading every
child document. Aim for ≤ {{ overview_max_tokens }} tokens.

Include, in this order:
- One-sentence summary of what this directory represents.
- Bullet list of the most important children (entity, episode, or fact),
  each with their source_uri on a new line.
- A short "Relationships" paragraph noting how the children connect — use
  the extracted RELATES_TO edges for this. Call out contradictions or
  supersessions.
- A short "Open questions" list if there are aspects the children do not cover.

Directory URI: {{ directory_uri }}

Children:
{% for c in children_abstracts %}
- {{ c.source_uri }}
  {{ c.abstract }}
{% endfor %}

Relationships (subject  --relation-->  object):
{% for r in children_relations %}
- {{ r.subject_uri }}  --{{ r.relation }}-->  {{ r.object_uri }}
{% endfor %}

Output schema:
{ "overview": "full markdown overview text" }
